## What exists

Corpus (12 October 2026). 525 CC0 sound effects, taken from seven Kenney packs (interface, impact, ui, digital, sci-fi, rpg, casino). Each pack's `License.txt` was read, and `prepare` refuses any pack whose licence does not say CC0. The files were downloaded without a login into `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design-refcache/sound-calibration/raw`. Each one is decoded to mono at 48 kHz, trimmed, capped at 1 s and peaked at -6 dB, then written to `prepared/`. The B1 rule tree (describe, extra, classify) assigns the class. Every file is listed in `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design-refcache/sound-calibration/manifest.json` with its source URL, licence, licence file, source sha256, class and the reason for that class. Class counts: click 100, impact 98, whoosh 44, keyboard 43, swoosh 39, blip 37, pop 30, swipe 29, glitch 19, boom 19, trigger 18, ding 18, tick 17, reverse 7, shimmer 6, subdrop 1. None of this is in the workshop.

OneKey targets (analysis only, 12 October 2026). The windows E001, E005, E006 and E007 of V_017 `events.json` are cut from the demucs stem each event was detected on, into `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design-refcache/onekey-pro-2/sound-targets/` (plus `manifest.json`). They are never archived, never published and never used as a deliverable.

Script: `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/ZenRayMotionDesign/Scripts/CalibrateSoundBank.py`, with steps `prepare | targets | fit | report | check`. All its parameters live in `datasets/sfx-params.json`, section `calibrate`.

- `fit` picks a stratified, deterministic subset of 180 sounds (12 per class, then round robin). It then runs four stages, and any sound already at 99 skips the remaining stages:
  1. A screen of every source block (a random pre-screen plus 40 Adam steps).
  2. A full dfit on the 4 best screened blocks.
  3. Pairs: the best single block, warm-started, layered with the next 2.
  4. An fx stage: the best chain followed by reverb_fdn, saturation or peak_eq.

  Fits are cached in `fits.jsonl`, keyed by sound, chain, the sha256 of each `block.py` and the settings, so a rerun only fits new chains. The step reports the score distribution per class, the best chains, the median error per loss term, the official ploss score beside the fitted metric, and a seed ceiling: the best chain scored against itself rendered with every noise seed moved by one.
- `fit --targets-only` (added 12 October 2026) fits only the four OneKey windows.
- `report --lines A:B` (added 12 October 2026) rebuilds a report from a slice of `fits.jsonl`. See "Defect found" below for why it was needed.
- `--out name.json` writes the report to a named file inside the calibration folder.

