What moved. The overall median rose from 82.29 to 87.87 on the fitted metric, and from 47.22 to 62.88 on the official A0 metric (official max 81.84 to 90.14). Every class gained or held; keyboard gained the most (42 to 65), then whoosh (77 to 87), reverse (77 to 86), glitch (70 to 79). Four sounds now pass 99 on the fitted metric, all slow sci-fi engine drones (boom, tick, trigger classes), fitted by `gated_tone` or `room_tone` layered with `wind` or `pad_saw`; their official scores are 72 to 90, so they are not 99 to the ear yet. Blip did not move at all (85.95 in both runs): no new block reached it.

Every class is still under 99 at the median, and every seed ceiling median is 98.2 or above, so the remaining gap is still a modelling gap. The missing block list from run 2 stands, reordered by run 4 error: keyboard and glitch need a multi-hit or stepped-gate source (envelope error 3.4 and 2.9 JND, the largest); ding and pop need inharmonic modal partials with per-partial decay and a body pitch drop (mel 3.3 and 3.1); blip needs a chip pulse with discrete pitch steps (stft 3.0, no progress); swoosh, whoosh, swipe and reverse need a noise band with breakpoint trajectories for centre and width (mel 2.2 to 2.7). The OneKey windows were not refitted (their 16 cached fits were reused; run 3 numbers stand).

Next: build those four block families in the bank, then rerun `fit --out calibration-report-run5.json`; with the pinned key only the new blocks are fitted.
